us.yaml and fr.yaml in this directory: squeekboard's terminal keyboard
layouts (US QWERTY and French AZERTY) with an Esc key, for terminals on the
SM-T715's on-screen keyboard.

License: GPL-3.0-or-later (SPDX header in each file). The text of the license
is in /usr/share/licenses/spdx/GPL-3.0-or-later.txt (Arch's licenses
package) and at https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.txt.

Origin of us.yaml: squeekboard 1.43.1, data/keyboards/terminal/us.yaml
(https://gitlab.gnome.org/World/Phosh/squeekboard, tag v1.43.1,
GPL-3.0-or-later), with an Esc key added by omarchy-mobile
(https://github.com/derekross/omarchy-mobile, commit 5f7ba48,
packages/omamobile-shell/squeekboard/keyboards/terminal/us.yaml). Shipped
unmodified by omarchy-tab-s2.

Origin of fr.yaml: squeekboard 1.43.1, data/keyboards/terminal/fr.yaml (the
copy built into Arch Linux ARM's squeekboard 1.43.1-6), with the same Esc
key added by omarchy-tab-s2 (the change is described in its header).

omarchy-tab-s2 ships both in image/rootfs/overlay/usr/share/t715-omarchy/; its
build links them as alarm's
~/.local/share/squeekboard/keyboards/terminal/{us,fr}.yaml, the only place
squeekboard reads layouts from besides its built-in ones.
